The histograms show two sets of test scores. For each dataset, decide whether it could be normally distributed. Give reasons.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=4mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\begin{scope}
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,9);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(7.7,0);
\foreach \x/\h in {1/1,2/3,3/6,4/8,5/6,6/3,7/1} {\draw[black] (\x-0.5,0) rectangle (\x+0.5,\h); \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {0,2,4,6,8} {\draw[black] (-0.12,\y)--(0,\y); \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.12,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[rotate=90] at (-2,4.5) {Frequency};
\node[below] at (4,-1.8) {Score};
\node[above] at (4,9) {Dataset A};
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[yshift=-65mm]
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,9);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(7.7,0);
\foreach \x/\h in {1/8,2/6,3/4,4/3,5/2,6/1,7/1} {\draw[black] (\x-0.5,0) rectangle (\x+0.5,\h); \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {0,2,4,6,8} {\draw[black] (-0.12,\y)--(0,\y); \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.12,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[rotate=90] at (-2,4.5) {Frequency};
\node[below] at (4,-1.8) {Score};
\node[above] at (4,9) {Dataset B};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Three normal curves are drawn on the same axes and scale.

(a) Which curve has the largest mean?

(b) Which curve has the largest standard deviation?

(c) Which two curves have the same mean?

(d) Which two curves have the same standard deviation?

Give reasons.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{mmblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{mmred}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[black,->] (-0.4,0)--(12,0);
\node[below] at (6,-0.15) {Score};
\draw[black,thick,domain=0:6,samples=121,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2.4*exp(-((\x-3)*(\x-3))/0.72)});
\draw[mmblue,thick,dashed,domain=-0.2:6.2,samples=121,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{1.2*exp(-((\x-3)*(\x-3))/2.88)});
\draw[mmred,thick,dotted,domain=6:12,samples=121,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2.4*exp(-((\x-9)*(\x-9))/0.72)});
\node[above] at (3,2.4) {$A$};
\node[text=mmblue,anchor=west] at (4.1,0.95) {$B$};
\node[text=mmred,above] at (9,2.4) {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
